00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:04.180
The big thing to consider about Joffrey in
season 4 is that there’s really one big

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.800
thing he has in the books.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.130
So what is the show going to do to expand
his part.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.770
Which starts our list off with...

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:13.860
Number 5 - Extra scenes.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.580
Because Joffrey isn’t a POV character in
book 3 but on the show he’s a main character

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:27.280
they had to change a lot of scenes so that
they were told from his perspective.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.399
That’s how a lot of characters get scenes
that weren’t originally in the books.

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:38.420
This will happen again in season 4 because
Joffrey has some big surprises headed his

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.560
way.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:50.420
Extra scenes also allow for the actors to
improvise things.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:57.890
Like this (insert joffrey sansa wedding scene
- tyrion).

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.510
Number 4 - More malevolence.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.030
Joffrey will continue to get even more evil.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:12.800
Even though Joffrey isn’t a targaryen he
is on the same path as the mad kings.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:18.280
He’s even the product of sisterwiving which
also happened with a lot of the targaryens.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:23.840
So as the series has progressed he’s gotten
crazier and crazier.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:30.760
There was that moment at the end of season
3 when it almost seemed like Tywin was going

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:39.500
to jump across the table and strangle him
to death, but the show was fairly true to

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:42.150
the book and it just ended in this amazing
tense moment.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.110
Number 3 - The rains of castamere.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:51.799
So if you remember, the song was turned into
the Lannister theme on the show.

00:02:51.799 --> 00:02:57.819
Whenever a lannister character is on screen
it plays really softly in the background,

00:02:57.819 --> 00:03:01.560
but during scenes like the red wedding it’s
literally played by characters.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:08.750
That’s not going to happen during Joffrey’s
wedding to margeary, but I’m really hoping

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:15.469
that the song plays softly in the background
during the wedding feast.

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:20.489
Number 2 - The Purple Wedding.

00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:23.120
Even if you haven’t read the books you may
have heard the term ‘The Purple Wedding’.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.530
It’s the name fans have affectionatly given
to Joffrey’s wedding to Margeary.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:32.470
It’s called the purple wedding because sansa
wears a hair hairnet covered in amethysts,

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:33.470
which are purple.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:38.319
And she unintentionally plays a big role in
Joffrey’s wedding.

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:42.409
Number 1 - The purple wedding feast and the
aftermath.

00:03:42.409 --> 00:04:06.489
So not only is the feast going to be one of
the most talked about moments on television

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:10.099
next year, from a production standpoint it’s
one of the most epic scenes the show has filmed.

00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:13.519
The scene was shot over a five day period
and included more principal cast members than

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.099
almost any other scene they’ve ever done.

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:18.060
There were 23 regular cast members and over
218 extras on set.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:27.370
Don’t be surprised if HBO promotes next
season using “Save The Date” invitations.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:32.300
But let me know what you’re biggest questions
for joffrey in season 4 are and what you’re

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.470
